cache/
data/raw/*
data/processed/*

# The OCR'd certificates. parse_coo_scan.py reads 448 scanned C of O PDFs that
# DOB BIS serves as images, and CI cannot regenerate any of it: BIS 403s
# automation, and neither the PDFs nor this cache were ever in the repo. The
# 40 readable results reach the map through coo_parsed.json, which is tracked
# — but that file is one `parse_coo_pdf.py --all` away from being rewritten,
# and without this cache the only way back was to re-OCR the archive for half
# an hour on a machine that still had the PDFs. 95KB to make the merge
# reproducible from a clean checkout.
!data/processed/coo_ocr_cache.jsonl
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.venv/
node_modules/
map/dist/
.vercel
.env*

# The Google-derived enrichment is the one thing in data/raw that CI cannot
# regenerate: refresh-data.yml runs the sixteen pull scripts and none of them
# calls Places. So the sweep output is committed rather than ignored, and the
# loaders find it on a fresh clone and in Actions alike.
#
# Only the verified file. The older text-search names stay ignored until they
# have been re-run with address verification, because shipping a name we
# cannot audit is worse than shipping none — the panel titles the building
# with it.
!data/raw/google_current_use_[0-9]*.json

# The candidate cache too, at 4.5MB, and not because CI needs it — CI reads
# the results file. It is committed because it is the only thing that makes a
# ranking change free. The ranking has now changed twice, and both times the
# whole sweep was re-queried: once because the cache stored verdicts instead
# of candidates, and once because the cache was deleted during a two-building
# test and had never been committed. Roughly $85 of Places calls each time.
!data/raw/google_current_use_cache.json

# The verified hotel names too. These carry the address each one matched, so a
# wrong match can be found later — the August files did not, which is why they
# were left out and have now been deleted rather than committed. 576 verified
# names between these and the sweep.
!data/raw/google_hotel_names_[0-9]*.json
!data/raw/google_hclass_hotels_[0-9]*.json
